RUSTNUTS APPLICATION — ORIGINAL SOFTWARE LICENCE

Copyright (c) 2026 Jeff Ostler, in the original application material in which
copyright subsists and is owned by him. All rights reserved except as below.

1. Scope and retained ownership

"Original Software" means the original application source code and technical
documentation in this repository, only to the extent that the relevant rights
subsist and are owned by Jeff Ostler ("Jeff"). It includes his original
contributions to screens, business logic, build tooling and database definitions.
It excludes third-party code and fonts, separately owned contributions, club
branding and documents, member content and personal information. Ideas, facts
and functionality as such are not claimed as copyright by this notice.

Jeff retains his rights in the Original Software. This licence is permission to
use that material, not an assignment of ownership to or from anyone. File-level
notices and separately applicable licences must be respected. Repository or
account ownership, author metadata and AI assistance do not by themselves prove
ownership of every contribution. See docs/licensing/OWNERSHIP-SCHEDULE.md for
known evidence and unresolved rights questions.

Jeff retains control of the main application build and its development. This
does not limit the Club's rights below to maintain and modify its implementation
or to choose its own maintainers.

2. Permanent club licence, without a licence fee

Jeff grants Rustnuts Social Motorcycle Club Incorporated ("Club") a worldwide,
non-exclusive, perpetual, irrevocable and royalty-free licence under his rights
in the Original Software to use, copy, build, host, run, maintain, repair and
modify it for the Club's activities. These include membership, administration,
rides, communications, merchandise and public club information. No licence fee
is payable for these rights.

The Club may keep complete source copies, build instructions and dependency
records; distribute executable copies and updates to its users, including through
app stores; and deploy its website. It may authorise officers, volunteers and
replacement contractors to access, copy and modify the source solely to develop,
operate and maintain its implementation. It may give hosting providers and app
stores the permissions reasonably necessary to deliver that implementation.
The Club may choose any maintainer at any time without Jeff's further approval;
it need not wait until Jeff is unable to maintain the application.
These permissions do not grant independent reuse or sale for another organisation,
except where a separate licence, valid earlier permission or applicable law does.

The Club's licence lasts for the full duration of Jeff's applicable rights and
does not end because Jeff leaves the Club, changes office, ceases maintenance,
becomes unavailable or transfers those rights. Any transfer by Jeff is subject
to this licence. The Club's grant does not depend on signing any new document
or completing an ownership or operating schedule.

Original updates owned by Jeff and supplied for this Club application, and
contributions whose rights are later validly assigned to him for incorporation
into it, receive the same club licence automatically. This provision does not
itself assign any contributor's rights or require anyone to create future work.
New material owned by other contributors remains subject to their own rights
and permissions; modifying the application does not automatically transfer it
to Jeff.

3. Other use and valid earlier permissions

Jeff may reuse the Original Software he owns to develop, operate and license
separate versions for other clubs or customers, including commercially. He does
not need the Club's further permission to reuse his own software rights. This
does not authorise reuse of Club branding, documents, confidential material,
member content or personal information without the necessary separate rights
and permissions; third-party licences continue to apply.

Developing or licensing another version does not withdraw or reduce the Club's
permanent fee-free licence, source access, modification rights or freedom to
choose maintainers, and does not alter Jeff's maintenance undertaking below.
No licence fee becomes payable by the Club because another version exists.

Except for the club grant above, this notice grants no new permission to use,
redistribute, sublicense or sell Jeff's Original Software. Additional permission
requires Jeff's written agreement, unless applicable law, GitHub platform terms,
another applicable licence or a valid earlier permission already allows the use.

This notice accompanies the revision in which it first appears and later
revisions retaining it. It does not retroactively revoke, narrow or replace any
valid permission already granted, including any MIT permission applicable to
earlier copies of original application material. The historical scope of the
former root MIT notice remains unresolved; moving its text does not determine
that scope or turn previously licensed material into exclusively restricted code.

4. Third-party materials

Third-party materials retain their copyright, licence and notice requirements.
No restriction here limits permissions under those licences. The former root
Expo MIT notice is preserved verbatim at licenses/Expo-MIT.txt. See
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the existing component notices, including the font's
OFL notice. That inventory is not a completed release-compliance audit.

5. Club assets, member content and information

Club names, insignia, artwork and documents remain separate from this software
licence. The Club and other creators retain whatever rights they hold in them;
no branding or document rights are assigned or licensed by this notice. Member
and other contributor rights in their content also remain separate.

Software ownership gives Jeff no independent right to access, use, sell,
disclose or retain member information. Authorised access, privacy obligations
and individual rights apply independently of software ownership. Service-account
control and credentials are also separate; this notice grants no account access.

6. Costs, support and non-excludable rights

Jeff will maintain the application for the Club for as long as he is able. If he
becomes unable to do so, the Club may continue maintenance through anyone it
chooses, with its source, modification and use rights intact. This does not
promise particular new features, response times or uninterrupted availability.

The fee-free grant does not require Jeff to pay hosting, app-store, email, API or
other service charges. Any paid services need a separate agreement and do not
alter the permanent fee-free software licence. To the extent permitted
by law, the Original Software is provided as is, without warranties. Nothing in
this notice excludes rights or remedies that cannot lawfully be excluded.

Jeff has confirmed that the club chairman, sitting presidents and treasurers
signed the agreement and assignment supporting this arrangement. The signed
originals were not supplied for this review. The texts in docs/licensing/ are
review drafts to reconcile with those originals, not copies of signed instruments.
This notice does not create an assignment or enlarge the rights actually assigned.
Existing valid agreements and permissions remain preserved; see the licensing record.
